          "creator": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
          "description": "Baker's Hill also starting point of the 'zip line' where you hook yourself to a cable and rocket across a deep valley to the other side. A true adrenaline rush if there was one, as your life literally hands by a single thread! I'll pass this one on, thank you very much. The hut you see in the foreground is the starting point for the zipline. Incidentally, Filpinos obviously love their ziplines, I found several of these rides in Davao, Cebu, two in Bohol, and here in Puerto Princesa. In Cebu, the zipline was across tall buildings. In the horizon is the Puerto Princesa bay. (Puerto Princesa, Philippines, May 2013)",
